ared 10.100.125.0/24 network using pdns_recursor: it listens on its private address, answers inventory.internal with node2's address (10.100.125.11) via an authoritative-domain A record, and forwards all other queries to the working upstream resolver at 10.100.125.1. node2 and node3 (CentOS Stream 10) were repointed via NetworkManager (ipv4.dns=10.100.125.10, ignore-auto-dns=yes) to resolve through node1. Verified both the internal record and upstream resolution work end-to-end from node2/node3. Completed the mandatory restart protocol: captured boot_id baselines and DNS health on all three nodes, restarted node1, node2, and node3 one at a time (never concurrently), confirmed each node's boot_id changed after reboot, and confirmed DNS service/config/resolution fully recovered on each node before proceeding to the next.\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Inspected OS, IPs, and existing resolv.conf on node1/node2/node3\",\"Located VyOS 2026.04 dns forwarding config tree (authoritative-domain records) via templates since docs were outdated for this version\",\"Verified 10.100.125.1 is a working upstream DNS resolver from node2\",\"Configured node1: set service dns forwarding listen-address 10.100.125.10, allow-from 10.100.125.0/24, name-server 10.100.125.1, authoritative-domain inventory.internal records a @ address 10.100.125.11; committed and saved\",\"Verified pdns_recursor active and listening on 10.100.125.10:53; tested inventory.internal and google.com resolution directly against node1\",\"Reconfigured node2 and node3 NetworkManager connections (ipv4.dns=10.100.125.10, ipv4.ignore-auto-dns=yes) and reapplied\",\"Verified end-to-end resolution from node2 and node3 for both inventory.internal and an external domain\",\"Captured boot_id + DNS health baseline on all three nodes\",\"Rebooted node1, polled until reachable, confirmed changed boot_id and full DNS recovery\",\"Rebooted node2, polled until reachable, confirmed changed boot_id and persisted resolv.conf/resolution\",\"Rebooted node3, polled until reachable, confirmed changed boot_id and persisted resolv.conf/resolution\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"node1 answers inventory.internal with node2's address\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-576657d6328f49dd\"],\"summary\":\"dig @10.100.125.10 inventory.internal +short returned 10.100.125.11 (node2's address) before restart\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 forwards everything else upstream\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-576657d6328f49dd\",\"cmd-f41a6d7db4e0473d\"],\"summary\":\"dig @10.100.125.10 google.com +short returned public IPs; confirmed 10.100.125.1 works as upstream first\"},{\"requirement\":\"node2 and node3 configured to resolve through node1\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-5782bcd36cc44d65\",\"cmd-aac4d4d38cdb4cc5\"],\"summary\":\"resolv.conf on node2 and node3 shows nameserver 10.100.125.10 after nmcli reconfiguration\"},{\"requirement\":\"end-to-end resolution works from node2/node3 for internal record and upstream\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-1c7e05d9e98b4826\",\"cmd-4eb50ce8d47b48df\"],\"summary\":\"getent hosts inventory.internal returns 10.100.125.11; getent ahostsv4 google.com returns public IP on both node2 and node3\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 healthy baseline before restart\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-6678fb5a5d6e4f6b\"],\"summary\":\"boot_id ebd78841..., pdns-recursor active, dig against 10.100.125.10 resolving both internal and external names\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 restart acknowledgement and changed boot identity\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-664e1a3d19d643fe\",\"cmd-24b65b517ff24b7d\",\"cmd-72b8bc58ee7a4bc4\",\"cmd-b47060558c0144f6\"],\"summary\":\"reboot scheduled and acked, connection drops during reboot, then boot_id a70c766e... differs from baseline ebd78841...\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 post-restart recovery\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-0d25ba4241c848c3\"],\"summary\":\"pdns-recursor active, interface address present, dig resolves inventory.internal and google.com correctly post-reboot\"},{\"requirement\":\"node2 healthy baseline before restart\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-11b79eea7c6c46d7\"],\"summary\":\"boot_id 21de1f79..., getent hosts inventory.internal resolves correctly\"},{\"requirement\":\"node2 restart acknowledgement and changed boot identity\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-2576a9fdff604de8\",\"cmd-1c843934b0e541a8\"],\"summary\":\"reboot scheduled and acked; post-reboot boot_id fe5aacc5... differs from baseline 21de1f79...\"},{\"requirement\":\"node2 post-restart recovery\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-36ba48e5debb495c\"],\"summary\":\"resolv.conf still points at 10.100.125.10; inventory.internal and google.com resolve correctly post-reboot\"},{\"requirement\":\"node3 healthy baseline before restart\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-7546548a21fd4800\"],\"summary\":\"boot_id be303eb3..., getent hosts inventory.internal resolves correctly\"},{\"requirement\":\"node3 restart acknowledgement and changed boot identity\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-ea990faf5fbe4f2d\",\"cmd-85a9a35359cc404d\"],\"summary\":\"reboot scheduled and acked; post-reboot boot_id 5d548f9b... differs from baseline be303eb3...\"},{\"requirement\":\"node3 post-restart recovery\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-1b760d81c4694799\"],\"summary\":\"resolv.conf still points at 10.100.125.10; inventory.internal and google.com resolve correctly post-reboot\"}]}","structured_output":{"status":"completed","summary":"Configured node1 (VyOS) as the DNS resolver for the shared 10.100.125.0/24 network using pdns_recursor: it listens on its private address, answers inventory.internal with node2's address (10.100.125.11) via an authoritative-domain A record, and forwards all other queries to the working upstream resolver at 10.100.125.1. node2 and node3 (CentOS Stream 10) were repointed via NetworkManager (ipv4.dns=10.100.125.10, ignore-auto-dns=yes) to resolve through node1. Verified both the internal record and upstream resolution work end-to-end from node2/node3. Completed the mandatory restart protocol: captured boot_id baselines and DNS health on all three nodes, restarted node1, node2, and node3 one at a time (never concurrently), confirmed each node's boot_id changed after reboot, and confirmed DNS service/config/resolution fully recovered on each node before proceeding to the next.","actions_performed":["Inspected OS, IPs, and existing resolv.conf on node1/node2/node3","Located VyOS 2026.04 dns forwarding config tree (authoritative-domain records) via templates since docs were outdated for this version","Verified 10.100.125.1 is a working upstream DNS resolver from node2","Configured node1: set service dns forwarding listen-address 10.100.125.10, allow-from 10.100.125.0/24, name-server 10.100.125.1, authoritative-domain inventory.internal records a @ address 10.100.125.11; committed and saved","Verified pdns_recursor active and listening on 10.100.125.10:53; tested inventory.internal and google.com resolution directly against node1","Reconfigured node2 and node3 NetworkManager connections (ipv4.dns=10.100.125.10, ipv4.ignore-auto-dns=yes) and reapplied","Verified end-to-end resolution from node2 and node3 for both inventory.internal and an external domain","Captured boot_id + DNS health baseline on all three nodes","Rebooted node1, polled until reachable, confirmed changed boot_id and full DNS recovery","Rebooted node2, polled until reachable, confirmed changed boot_id and persisted resolv.conf/resolution","Rebooted node3, polled until reachable, confirmed changed boot_id and persisted resolv.conf/resolution"],"evidence":[{"requirement":"node1 answers inventory.internal with node2's address","command_ids":["cmd-576657d6328f49dd"],"summary":"dig @10.100.125.10 inventory.internal +short returned 10.100.125.11 (node2's address) before restart"},{"requirement":"node1 forwards everything else upstream","command_ids":["cmd-576657d6328f49dd","cmd-f41a6d7db4e0473d"],"summary":"dig @10.100.125.10 google.com +short returned public IPs; confirmed 10.100.125.1 works as upstream first"},{"requirement":"node2 and node3 configured to resolv